+
+## 14. Conversation list response
+
+`ConversationListMessage` describes a `conversation_list` frame whose rows are `ConversationSummary` values; `ListConversationsMessage` and `ConversationCursor` describe the request and cursor.
+
+| Field                        | Type   | Description                                           |
+| ---------------------------- | ------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`                       | string | `"conversation_list"`                                 |
+| `conversations`              | array  | Conversation summaries in newest-activity order       |
+| `conversations[].sessionId`  | string | Id usable with the existing `?sessionId=` resume path |
+| `conversations[].createdAt`  | string | ISO creation time                                     |
+| `conversations[].updatedAt`  | string | ISO activity time                                     |
+| `conversations[].entryCount` | number | Number of entries, without their content              |
+
+- The server answers only when asked, with one list and no `stream_end`; conversation metadata is personal data belonging only to the authenticated connection user, never the user named by a frame, and neither entries nor credentials are disclosed ([validated by: lists only the authenticated owner with wire dates, pages ties, and resumes a listed conversation](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L157)).
+- `transport.history` is the deployer's opt-in to making that metadata reachable by a client, independently of resume, and unavailable history produces `UNSUPPORTED` rather than an empty list ([validated by: refuses unavailable history with UNSUPPORTED and warns when history cannot be resumed](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L207)).
+
+The [conversation-list spec](../hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md#websocket-history-144) defines paging, failures and turn concurrency; retention remains the consumer's decision under #41, as with session resume.
